{"assets":["/statement-assets/2de7638569793ffeef781684fc811e06ab75d1e92e0af239d69b95bc3e930bd4.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1797","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Li Hua and Path"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Li Hua has a tree of $$$n$$$ vertices and $$$n-1$$$ edges. The vertices are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A pair of vertices $$$(u,v)$$$ ($$$u \\lt v$$$) is considered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cute"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the following two statements is true:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$u$$$ is the vertex with the minimum index among all vertices on the path $$$(u,v)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$v$$$ is the vertex with the maximum index among all vertices on the path $$$(u,v)$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There will be $$$m$$$ operations. In each operation, he decides an integer $$$k_j$$$, then inserts a vertex numbered $$$n+j$$$ to the tree, connecting with the vertex numbered $$$k_j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He wants to calculate the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cute"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs before operations and after each operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose you were Li Hua, please solve this problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains the single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2\\le n\\le 2\\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of vertices in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next $$$n-1$$$ lines contain the edges of the tree. The $$$i$$$-th line contains two integers $$$u_i$$$ and $$$v_i$$$ ($$$1\\le u_i,v_i\\le n$$$; $$$u_i\\ne v_i$$$) — the corresponding edge. The given edges form a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains the single integer $$$m$$$ ($$$1\\le m\\le 2\\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next $$$m$$$ lines contain operations — one operation per line. The $$$j$$$-th operation contains one integer $$$k_j$$$ ($$$1\\le k_j \\lt n+j$$$) — a vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$m+1$$$ integers — the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cute"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs before operations and after each operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n2 1\n1 3\n1 4\n4 6\n4 7\n6 5\n2\n5\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n11\n15\n19\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The initial tree is shown in the following picture:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2de7638569793ffeef781684fc811e06ab75d1e92e0af239d69b95bc3e930bd4.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$11$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cute"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs — $$$(1,5),(2,3),(2,4),(2,6),(2,7),(3,4),(3,6),(3,7),(4,5),(5,7),(6,7)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Similarly, we can count the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cute"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs after each operation and the result is $$$15$$$ and $$$19$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1797F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1797/problem/F"}